§§ `s 25 -- the right of access`

-- Arguments: held; collected on or after 1 July 2002; older record of a listed kind; FOI document; news medium; EPHISS;
-- privileged.
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `access in the way I ask under s 28`
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `an accurate summary, or more if the organisation agrees`
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `access only under the Freedom of Information Act 1982`
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no access under this Act`
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no access under this Act`
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `no access under this Act`
-- s 96 "Despite any other section": privilege wins over the FOI route of s 16.
#ASSERT `Do I have a right of access` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `no access under this Act`

§§ `ss 26, 27, 85(5), HPP 6.1, 6.2 -- must I be given access`

-- Arguments: right of access; serious threat; given in confidence; giver consented; other ground; evaluative commercial
-- information; representative may prejudice.
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation must give me access`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation must not give me access: a serious threat to life or health (s 26)`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation must not give me access: given in confidence (s 27)`
-- s 27(3): the giver consents, the bar lifts.
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `no ground` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation must give me access`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `unreasonable impact on other people's privacy (HPP 6.1(b))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation may refuse access on another HPP 6.1 ground`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a repeat of an unsuccessful request with no reasonable grounds (HPP 6.1(k))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation may refuse access on another HPP 6.1 ground`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `existing legal proceedings and not discoverable, or privileged (HPP 6.1(c))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation may refuse access on another HPP 6.1 ground`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ground` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the organisation may refuse my authorised representative (s 85(5))`
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no ground` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the organisation may give me an explanation instead (HPP 6.2)`
-- The "must not" of s 26 comes first.
#ASSERT `Must I be given access` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `existing legal proceedings and not discoverable, or privileged (HPP 6.1(c))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the organisation must not give me access: a serious threat to life or health (s 26)`

